%% Proposed sequence. Explicit saves are synchronous; optional indexes may lag.
sequenceDiagram
  actor A as User A / Jake
  participant GW as Trusted knowledge gateway
  participant SQL as Canonical ledger and source registry
  participant IDX as Optional shared index
  actor B as User B / Michael
  participant QA as Bounded question workflow
  participant UI as Inline answer

  A->>GW: Remember WELL-0007 planned work from 17 Oct for about ten days
  GW->>GW: Resolve subject, shared audience, plan kind, source and approximate period
  Note over GW,SQL: Preserve only the minimal domain assertion; private chat stays private
  GW->>SQL: Validate and commit claim, receipt, revision R+1 and outbox atomically
  SQL-->>GW: Durable claim ID and R+1
  GW-->>A: Saved shared plan with author and period
  SQL-->>IDX: Outbox projects sourced claim asynchronously

  B->>QA: Is any downtime planned for WELL-0007?
  QA->>GW: Trusted B context, subject and explicit reference date
  GW->>SQL: Read committed head R+1, exact shared subject plans and conflicts
  GW->>SQL: Load only B private capsule and entity receipts
  SQL-->>GW: Jake plan, applicable evidence and B own memory
  opt Semantic expansion is useful
    GW->>IDX: Authorized search with source scope and watermark
    IDX-->>GW: Candidates plus indexed-through revision
    GW->>SQL: Revalidate claims and union canonical deltas if index lags
  end
  GW-->>QA: B own context plus shared plan and evidence at R+1
  QA->>SQL: Persist one validated answer snapshot
  QA-->>UI: About ten days from 17 Oct, according to Jake
  Note over A,B: The shared claim is read once from shared storage, never copied from A private memory

  B->>QA: The three wells we discussed yesterday?
  QA->>GW: Resolve exact entity sets owned by B
  GW->>SQL: B history only; no fallback to A history
  SQL-->>GW: Absent if B has no such conversation
  QA-->>UI: Request the well IDs; do not inherit A discussion set
